## 3. Integration Example

```csharp
// Main program to demonstrate usage
class Program
{
    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Setup statistics (in real scenario, this would come from metadata)
        var statsManager = new StatisticsManager();
        statsManager.AddTable("customers", 1000000);
        statsManager.AddTable("orders", 5000000);
        statsManager.AddTable("products", 10000);

        // Create cost estimator
        var costEstimator = new CostEstimator(statsManager);

        // Create optimizer
        var optimizer = new Optimizer(costEstimator);

        // Parse SQL query
        var sql = "SELECT c.name, o.order_date, p.price FROM customers c JOIN orders o ON c.id = o.customer_id JOIN products p ON o.product_id = p.id WHERE o.order_date > '2023-01-01'";
        var parser = new SQLParser(sql);
        var ast = parser.Parse();

        // Optimize query
        var plan = optimizer.Optimize(ast);

        // Execute plan
        var context = new QueryContext();
        plan.Execute(context);

        // For distributed scenario
        var nodes = new List<DatabaseNode>
        {
            new DatabaseNode { Name = "node1", Statistics = statsManager },
            new DatabaseNode { Name = "node2", Statistics = statsManager }
        };

        var distributedOptimizer = new DistributedOptimizer(nodes);
        var distributedPlan = await distributedOptimizer.OptimizeAndExecute(ast);
    }
}
```

## 4. Key Features

1. **Modular Design**:
   - Clear separation between parsing, optimization, and execution
   - Each component can be replaced or extended independently

2. **Cost-Based Optimization**:
   - Evaluates join order permutations
   - Considers table statistics for accurate cost estimation
   - Supports different join algorithms (hash, merge, nested loop)

3. **Distributed Capabilities**:
   - Query sharding across nodes
   - Parallel execution
   - Result merging

4. **Extensibility**:
   - New node types can be added to AST
   - Additional optimization rules can be implemented
   - New physical operators can be added

